SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi & Agios Panteleimon\, Kattavia
LOCATION:Kattavia\, Rhodes\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The southernmost village of Rhodes runs a three-day panigiri from 25 to 27 July for both Agia Paraskevi and Agios Panteleimon\, with a glendi on the square each night and the Prasonisi kitesurf crowd mixing with the locals. Kattavia also feasts the Panagia on 14 August and holds a 'lopou' (local pulse) festival in late August. It is an hour and a half from Rhodes town\, so stay in Gennadi or Lachania rather than driving back.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#kattavia-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-agios-panteleimon-kattav
